      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the shift toward political messaging in contemporary art is a significant consequence of deconstructing traditional aesthetic hierarchies, it expands rather than diminishes the value of the art form by challenging viewers to engage critically. History shows that art has always served as a vehicle for social commentary, and prioritizing such ideas often fosters deeper conceptual resonance over mere visual appeal. This trend forces institutions and critics to rethink valuation criteria beyond craftsmanship, potentially leading to a more expansive yet demanding understanding of artistic merit. Ultimately, the increased focus on ideas has enriched artistic discourse but may inadvertently discourage audiences seeking purely sensory experiences.",
